  "name": "bloom-market",
  "vibe": "Blush #f6e7e9 paper with a magenta that behaves like a bloom rather than a brand colour. DM Serif Display sets headlines in sentence case; Albert Sans handles kickers and labels. Four stems grow from the bottom edge and sway on a slow sine, five ellipse petals turning around a butter-yellow centre, while loose petals spin down the frame at 55% opacity — the backdrop is a stall, not a pattern. Cards land tilted with an ink outline and pill chips in magenta, leaf and butter; one beat floods full magenta with butter type, and the stats beat drops to near-black #322a2e. Its owned mechanics are drag-to-arrange, a switch list, a dragged slider and an arc gauge. Best for florists, farmers markets, bakeries, artisan retail and seasonal subscription boxes.",
